<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Neuhaus Foot & Ankle collects, uses and protects information when you use our website.">
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Neuhaus Foot &amp; Ankle ("we", "us") handles information when you visit
    this website. It covers the website only. How we handle your medical records is described in our
    <a class="underline" href="/notice-of-privacy-practices">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Information you give us.</strong> If you call us, email us or book through an online scheduling link, you may share your name, phone number, email and the reason for your visit.</li>
    <li><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, we may receive your IP address, browser type, device type, the pages you view and the date and time of your visit.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies.</strong> We may use cookies and similar tools to keep the site working and to understand how it is used.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer your questions and help you book appointments.</li>
    <li>To run, secure and improve our website.</li>
    <li>To understand which pages are useful so we can make them better.</li>
    <li>To follow the law and protect our rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Please do not send medical details through the website</h2>
  <p>
    Regular email and website messages may not be secure. Do not send sensitive health details this way.
    Call your office or use our patient portal for private health questions. If you have a medical emergency,
    call 911.
  </p>

  <h2>Online booking and other services</h2>
  <p>
    Appointment booking is handled by Healow, and online bill payment and the patient portal are run by
    other companies. When you click those links you leave this website and their own privacy terms apply.
    We are not responsible for the privacy practices of other websites.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing information</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information. We may share it with companies that help us run the website
    (for example hosting and analytics), when the law requires it, or to protect the safety and rights of
    our patients, staff and the public.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Some parts of the site may work less well if you do.
    If your browser sends a "Do Not Track" or Global Privacy Control signal, we will respect it where the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>We keep website information only as long as we need it for the purposes above or as the law requires.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable steps to protect information. No website or internet service is completely secure,
    so we cannot promise absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is meant for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13
    through the website. A parent or guardian should make appointments for a child.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask us what information we hold from your website use, ask us to correct or delete it, or ask us to
    stop contacting you. Contact us using the details below. Rights over your medical records are explained in the
    Notice of Privacy Practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
</LegalLayout>
